  "postCreationUserMessage": {
    "required": true,
    "template": "global_commands: Agentlas terminal/app plain language through native Agentlas/Hephaestus tools; Claude Code /hep-build, /hep-network, /hep-local, /hep-cloud, /hep-hub, /hep-search, /hep-browser, /hep-call, /hep-upload, /hep-graph, /hep-connect; current Codex $hephaestus-build, $hephaestus-network, $hephaestus-cloud, $hephaestus-storm, $hephaestus-graph and plain language for other MCP surfaces; Gemini CLI, Antigravity, Cursor, and OpenCode expose /hep-build, /hep-network, /hep-local, /hep-cloud, /hep-hub, /hep-search, /hep-browser, /hep-call, /hep-upload, /hep-graph. Antigravity is installed independently; Gemini CLI is only an optional additional host. Workforce scopes: network = registered Local + owner Cloud + public Hub; local = registered Local only; cloud = signed-in owner Cloud only; hub = public Hub only. All four use local MCP server hephaestus-network and the exact workforce.search_candidates -> workforce.validate_selection -> workforce.prepare_execution contract. On local-OS hosts it is the only Workforce MCP; Core performs Cloud/Hub upstream calls internally and direct agentlas MCP registration is removed to prevent duplicate tools from bypassing federation and privacy governance. Other meanings: build/create = /hep-build; automation = /hep-graph; search-only = /hep-search; browser-required = /hep-browser; explicit named call = /hep-call; upload gate = /hep-upload; Telegram setup = /hep-connect or plain-language Codex MCP request; force-robust completion = /hep-storm (Codex $hephaestus-storm)."
  }
